WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.325
The usual answer is to buy our way out.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:07.350
ServiceNow sells compliance and
continuous-authorization applications that do much

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.034
of this, and identity-governance
products such

4
00:00:10.034 --> 00:00:12.650
as SailPoint run access
reviews and a lot more.

5
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.288
Microsoft has its own
governance features too.

6
00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:18.834
But ServiceNow's own documentation
lists those compliance

7
00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:22.949
applications as separate subscriptions,
on top of what we already pay.

8
00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:26.154
An identity-governance product
is another purchase again,

9
00:00:26.154 --> 00:00:28.900
and Microsoft's features
need their own licensing.

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.150
If the answer on funding is
no, we have two choices.

11
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.668
We can leave the design on paper
and keep doing things by email,

12
00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:39.600
or we can build the essential pieces
ourselves on what we already own.

13
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.180
This briefing is about the
second choice, done carefully.
